  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "It was suggested a while back to use AvatarRoot as a replacement to the old GetRotation behavior before the FBT \"jitter\" issue was resolved.\n\nWhen using it directly with TeleportTo it produces the correct behavior for Desktop, however, with VR it causes some awkward issues that don't appear to be documented.\n\n3 Point VR is generally fine in most cases but can cause some weird rotations to occur when tilting or looking at certain angles.\n\nIn FBT (4+ Point Tracking) this has massive issues where the player feels locked in their head rotation but when looking down it's more free. This is problematic with worlds not using the TrackingData Origin method with a bit of transformation math.\n\nPossible Solutions:\n\nCreate a `GetControllerRotation` method or similar name to pull a rotation that works well with passing as a TeleportTo rotation (using Head as reference since that is the default in the Scene Descriptor). Thorough docs can be added to specify usage to allow a player to only be teleported positionally. This would both achieve the old behavior and allow current systems that have adapted to continue working, however, this doesn't fully solve the issue since it just provides an alternative that's easier to use.\n\nCreate `SetPosition` and `SetRotation` methods to perform a similar TeleportTo but only controlling either the position or the rotation (still containing Interpolate on Remote flag). This would be the best option for Udon and remove the need to rely on TrackingData. This still leaves the issues with avatar systems though. I have not tested if there is a good alternative for avatars, please comment one if there is!\n\nAdjust the AvatarRoot behavior for VR to provide a more stable usage with TeleportTo and Avatar systems. This would be fixing the issues with 3 Point VR's head tilting and FBT's sudden rotations upon movement. This could effect some current avatar systems but it appears the majority currently suffer from the current \"snapping\" FBT behavior.\n\nVideo Context:\n\nSquare = TrackingData Origin\n\nCircle = VRCPlayerApi GetRotation\n\nTriangle = TrackingData AvatarRoot",
